## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1 — Critical (P0) 🔴

Exploitable vulnerabilities — fix immediately.

---

#### 1.1 Tighten CORS on ALL Edge Functions

**Problem**: Every single edge function (47+ files) sets `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: '*'`. Any website on the internet can make authenticated cross-origin requests to your Supabase functions if a user has an active session.

**Affected files**: All files in [supabase/functions/](file:///e:/promptline-new/promptline-secure/supabase/functions) — confirmed 47+ `index.ts` files with `'*'`.

##### [NEW] `supabase/functions/_shared/cors.ts`
Shared CORS utility with environment-aware origin allowlist:
```typescript
const ALLOWED_ORIGINS = [
  // Production
  'https://secure.promptline.app',
  'https://admin.promptline.app',
  // Sandbox
  'https://secure.sandbox.promptline.app',
  'https://admin.sandbox.promptline.app',
  // Local dev
  'http://localhost:5173',
  'http://localhost:5174',
];

export function corsHeaders(req: Request) {
  const origin = req.headers.get('Origin') ?? '';
  const allowed = ALLOWED_ORIGINS.includes(origin) ? origin : '';
  return {
    'Access-Control-Allow-Origin': allowed,
    'Access-Control-Allow-Headers': 'authorization, x-client-info, apikey, content-type',
    'Access-Control-Allow-Methods': 'GET,POST,PUT,DELETE,OPTIONS',
  };
}
```

##### [MODIFY] 47+ edge function `index.ts` files
Replace every hardcoded CORS header object with `corsHeaders(req)` from the shared module.

**Note**: Functions called by **external services** (e.g., `eleven-post-call` called by ElevenLabs, `paypal-webhook` called by PayPal, `sms-inbound` called by Twilio) don't need CORS at all since they're server-to-server. For those, CORS headers can be removed entirely and replaced with signature verification.

