#### 1.2 API Server Authentication & Webhook Verification

**Problem**: The Fastify API server ([index.js](file:///e:/promptline-new/promptline-api/index.js) — 1889 lines) has **no global authentication**. Routes like incoming calls accept tenantId from the request body without verifying the caller. Webhook endpoints (Twilio, ElevenLabs) don't verify request signatures.

##### [NEW] `promptline-api/middleware/webhookAuth.js`
Webhook signature verification middleware:
- **Twilio**: Use `twilio.validateRequest(authToken, signature, url, params)` on `/incoming-call`, `/status-callback`, all SMS routes
- **ElevenLabs**: Verify HMAC signature on `/eleven-post-call` webhook using `ELEVEN_SECRET`

##### [MODIFY] [index.js](file:///e:/promptline-new/promptline-api/index.js)
- Add `preHandler` hooks on webhook routes for signature verification
- Add origin/API-key check on app-initiated routes (calls from Secure/Admin)
- Keep public health-check routes unprotected

---

#### 1.3 Input Validation

**Problem**: Request bodies across edge functions and the API server accept user input (phone numbers, emails, tenant IDs, business data) without thorough schema validation. While Supabase parameterizes queries, unvalidated input can still cause logic bugs and data integrity issues.

##### [MODIFY] Edge functions (prioritized list)
Add validation for all request bodies in security-sensitive functions:
- `paypal-charge`, `paypal-vault-card`, `paypal-refund` — validate amounts, tenant IDs
- `tenant-profile` — validate phone (E.164), email format, field lengths
- `agents` — validate configuration objects
- `send-sms-with-link`, `send-ms-email` — validate recipient addresses
- `contacts` — validate contact data fields

##### [MODIFY] [index.js](file:///e:/promptline-new/promptline-api/index.js)
- Add JSON schema validation for Fastify routes (Fastify has built-in schema support)
- Validate all phone numbers match E.164 format: `/^\+1\d{10}$/`
- Validate UUIDs for tenant/business IDs

